        "background_color": "#f5f1eb"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "checklist": {
          "type": "custom-liquid",
          "settings": {
            "custom_liquid": "<div class=\"at-checklist\"><div class=\"at-checklist__intro\"><p class=\"at-checklist__eyebrow\">Start here</p><h2 id=\"first-line\" class=\"at-checklist__title\">What your first line needs</h2></div><ol class=\"at-checklist__items\"><li><strong>One hero tee</strong><p>Pick the tee people will know you for and start it in 2 or 3 colors.</p></li><li><strong>A matching layer</strong><p>Add a hoodie or a crew, not both at first, in the same colors as the tee.</p></li><li><strong>One add-on for your customer</strong><p>Long sleeve, a women&rsquo;s cut, youth sizes, a tank or a hat. Choose the one your buyers will ask for.</p></li><li><strong>Grow in the same brand</strong><p>Add a zip hoodie, joggers or new colors from the same line so fit and shades stay consistent.</p></li></ol><p class=\"at-checklist__note\"><strong>Why stay in one brand?</strong> Sizing, fabric and dye change from mill to mill. Keeping your core pieces in one brand means a customer who knows their size in your tee can order your hoodie with confidence, and your colors line up side by side.</p></div>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "checklist"
      ]
    },
